Zero OS 0.9.0 final VM verification — PASS
Date: 2026-11-16 UTC.
Exact tested image: build/zero.iso, 18,890,752 bytes.
SHA256: 880feb36e9c95d26abd0adaf912668396b1c135b98a04e4d87fa996ca8a90a05

All four complete runs passed: BIOS32 (long mode and PAE disabled), BIOS64,
UEFI32, UEFI64. All VMs stopped; the ISO and all private test disk copies
retain their initial complete SHA256. Each framebuffer is native 1920x1080.
QEMU TCG/PCnet user networking, not native VirtualBox or physical hardware.
Actual argv, serial transcripts, command outputs, PCAP and results are saved
per mode. matrix.json summarizes the exact assertions.

Before any terminal input, each guest independently completed real DHCP
Discover/Offer/Request/ACK. net reported IP 10.0.2.15, mask 255.255.255.0,
gateway 10.0.2.2 and DNS 10.0.2.3. Link loss cleared the addresses; restoring
the virtual cable caused automatic DHCP recovery without a reconnect command.
This recovery and local HTTP 200 completed with compute thread 3 paused.
Both its block counter and checksum stayed unchanged; they advanced on resume.
Independent packet decoding found no bad guest IPv4 or TCP checksums.

Visible task numbers are 1 terminal, 2 graphics and 3 computation. pause 0/1/4
was rejected. Pausing graphics preserved every framebuffer byte while terminal
commands continued, and resume redrew the framebuffer. While graphics was
paused, pixel 1 1 and pixel 1920 1080 modified exactly the first/last physical
pixels. Zero and coordinates beyond width/height were rejected; a full-image
comparison verified that no other pixels changed.

Each guest made two real HTTP requests to the independent local HTTP/1.0
fixture: directly to 10.0.2.2, and after public DNS resolution of
10.0.2.2.nip.io to 10.0.2.2. These establish guest DNS plus local HTTP, not
public Internet HTTP access. The separate host example.com:80 probe failed
with errno 101 (Network is unreachable); external HTTP is unverified.

The production wifi command opened the no-adapter modal. Actual PS/2 Up,
Down, F1, F5, q and Enter did not leak input or modify that modal. Escape
restored the shell and window/focus state. WIRELESS header pixels were checked
against the own font. BIOS read-only memory snapshots additionally verified
terminal history preservation and zeroed WiFi password storage. No native
WiFi radio, scanning, authentication or association was tested or claimed.
Stock QEMU has no WiFi radio; hosted UI simulations are separate evidence.

In each mode, 15 native compiler/help invocations and a subsequent terminal
command passed: Zero output and nonzero exit; Ezero text, math, typed phrase
fields and repeat; Zero malformed-source rejection; actual Ezero line/reason
diagnostic; Ezero zero-index runtime error/exit 65; full-u64 store/load; stdin
EOF; exactly 4095 output bytes with exit 74 on overflow; and successful Ezero
compilation/execution after all errors. These use the default bundled native
compilers and real PS/2 source input, not host compilation substituted for
guest execution. Network and tasks remained usable afterwards. Guest programs
remain cooperative and share kernel address space; no isolation guarantee.

Read-only storage regression used newly copied private fixtures, never the
user's build/data.img or build/data.vdi. disks used one-based disk labels;
read B:|welcome and GO B:| followed by read welcome returned the ext4 fixture
text. Full SHA256 of both private disks remained unchanged in every mode.
This is a read regression, not a fresh full filesystem write/crash suite.

55 recorded command/control actions per BIOS mode, 58 per UEFI mode: 226
records total. This is a focused behavioral and boundary matrix, not 100
arbitrary repetitions and not proof that every possible bug is absent.
Earlier candidate failures remain under their different ISO hashes. In
particular the paused-computation bug in 1cff88fb was fixed and its actual
counter/checksum behavior is now independently verified in all four modes.

Reproduce from repository root:
python3 verification/network-0.9.0/run.py --iso build/zero.iso --sha \
880feb36e9c95d26abd0adaf912668396b1c135b98a04e4d87fa996ca8a90a05 \
--label NEW_UNIQUE_LABEL --guest-compilers --storage

Evidence screenshots are native captures, never resized. wifi-no-adapter.png
is the production no-radio screen; native-compilers.png includes the deliberate
long-output boundary test and is not a curated compiler demonstration.
